  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated response to address health, nutrition and protection needs of older people and persons with specific needs in Gambella</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved access to lifesaving nutrition and reduction in all forms of malnutrition among 3,400 (1,926 female &amp; 1,474 male) older women and men</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved health status of 22,397 (11,783 female and 10,614 male) PSNs, including older people and PwDs</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved protection and inclusion of 16,895 (9,052 female and 7,843 male) older women and men, PwDs and PSN</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to increase the wellbeing and dignity of PSNs, including older people and PwDs in Gambella by providing a tailored and integrated response to address their health, nutrition and protection needs. The project will benefit a total of 42,500 individuals in seven refugee camps and the local host communities.</narrative>
  </description>
